In addition, Fund managers may impose a Dilution Levy to share out the costs incurred when a need to deal in underlying assets is triggered by investor purchases or redemptions of Fund units/shares. This may also apply to Structured Products. This is to prevent these costs diluting the value of units/shares held by continuing investors. Any charge arising from a Dilution Levy being applied will either be reflected in the offer price of the units or be applied as a levy to the amount invested or disinvested.
