es it need to, because the recommended product is not complex. The absence of a formal knowledge/experience assessment grading in the file (noted in the extraction metadata) means that dimension cannot be corroborated; however, the mislabeling of the product itself is a material discrepancy between the report's assertion and the file's evidence of what the product is.","citations":[{"passageId":"P1","source":"H_Key_Features","category":"H","quote":"You can choose to take your retirement benefits in one of the following ways: take all of your pension pot as a cash lump sum. Up to 25% will be paid tax free...take up to 25% of your pension pot tax free as a lump sum and/or as a regular income, and then take the remaining pension pot as and when you need it through drawdown...use your entire pension pot to purchase an annuity...take up to 25% of your pension pot tax free and use the remaining pension pot to purchase a smaller annuity.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"I_Suitability_Report","category":"I","quote":"An individual can take up to 25% of the pension fund being crystallised as a tax-free lump sum at outset (subject to the Lump Sum Allowance of £268,275 for people with no form of lifetime allowance protection). The remainder of the fund remains invested within a tax advantaged environment from which the individual can take regular or ad-hoc income withdrawals to suit their needs and circumstances.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"H_Fund_Factsheet","category":"H","quote":"The Fund seeks to provide long term growth (combining capital and income) consistent with a balanced volatility level over the long term. The Fund is actively managed...Typically, the Fund will maintain an exposure to equities of between 30% - 70% of the portfolio, which in the investment manager's view, is consistent with the Fund's aim to maintain a balanced volatility level.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P20","source":"H_Key_Features","category":"H","quote":"To give you the flexibility and a range of options to control how your retirement pension pot is invested...To give you the control and flexibility to manage your benefits in retirement...You should retain the services of a financial adviser.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"H_Fund_Factsheet","category":"H","quote":"Fund type: UK UCITS...Comparator benchmark: IA Mixed Investment 40-85% Shares...Ongoing charge: 0.29%","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Data inconsistency","Weak justification"],"severity":"Moderate","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

