ecific fees documented."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The requirement tests whether the suitability report states, for each change suggested, whether it is recommended, who will implement it, and the intended outcome. The report satisfies the structural requirement: each of the five recommendations explicitly states (a) adviceStatus of 'Recommended', (b) implementation responsibility (Client for Retain, Adviser for all others), and (c) a specific intended outcome naming client objectives (consolidation, risk alignment, flexibility, tax efficiency). The implementation field contains the next steps including timescale (10-15 working days), processing considerations (out-of-market risk disclosure, cancellation rights), and adviser fees. The report is internally consistent: all five actions are marked as Recommended; the adviser accepts implementation responsibility for all changes except the Retain action, which requires no adviser action; and each outcome is stated in terms linked to client objectives stated elsewhere in the report (consolidation, risk management, flexibility). The requirement does not mandate that the file hold independent evidence corroborating each recommendation; it asks whether the report contains the statement. The suitability report itself contains the statement. The file's silence on these recommendations — it holds no adviser letter, no instruction, no change authorization — is not a contradiction of what the report says; it is an absence of corroboration. The report's internal consistency between the five recommendations, their status, implementation responsibility, and intended outcomes is complete. No guard applies: these are not 'You may wish to consider' suggestions (they are unambiguously recommended); the report does state who will implement each (the adviceStatus and implementation fields are explicit); and the intended outcomes are clearly named for each. The canonical model extraction captured the report's statements accurately. No discrepancy exists between what the report asserts and what it asserts elsewhere. The question is whether the report contains the required statement: it does.","citations":[{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model: /recommendations[]/adviceStatus","category":null,"quote":"[\"Recommended\", \"Recommended\", \"Recommended\", \"Recommended\", \"Recommended\"]","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model: /recommendations[]/implementation/willAdviserImplement","category":null,"quote":"[false, true, true, true, true]","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model: /recommendations[]/implementation/responsibleParty","category":null,"quote":"[\"Client\", \"Adviser\", \"Adviser\", \"Adviser\", \"Adviser\"]","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model: /recommendations[]/intendedOutcome","category":null,"quote":"[\"Continue to benefit from employer contributions while maintaining current investment performance\", \"Simplify pension arrangements while minimizing tax impact\", \"Consolidate pension arrangements, escape lifestyling funds that move outside agreed risk range, and gain greater investment flexibility\", \"Consolidate largest pension holding, gain appropriate risk-level funds, and improve retirement flexibility\", \"Consolidate pension arrangements, escape lifestyling funds, and ensure investment remains aligned with agreed risk profile\"]","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model: /solution/implementation/expectedTimescale","category":null,"quote":"\"10-15 working days for administration, disinvestment and banking processes\"","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model: /solution/implementation/nextSteps[4]/text","category":null,"quote":"\"For researching, recommending and arranging these investments, we charge an initial advice fee of 3% of the amount invested as per the terms stated in our Client Agreement. In monetary terms this is £3,305.55 with current tran