## Conflict of Interest
To ensure that clients' interests are always put first, we operate a conflicts of interest policy.  If a potential conflict of interest does arise it will be actively managed, and we have arrangements in place to ensure that all our clients are treat fairly. We will, where appropriate, notify you of conflicts and/ or obtain your consent to proceed.
## Complaint Procedure
If you are not happy with the service you have received you can request a copy of our complaints procedure  that  sets  out  how we will  handle your complaint.  Please  refer  to our ' Important Information about our Services' document for further details on how you can make a complaint.
## Financial Service Compensation Scheme
Under the Financial Services Compensation Scheme ( FSCS ), if we or any other firm to whom we have introduced you , are unable to meet our obligations, you may be entitled to compensation.
The current limits, which are subject to change, that can be paid out by the FSCS are:
Investments- most types of investment business are covered for 100% of the claim up to a maximum of £85,000.
Long-term insurance benefits (e.g. pensions and life assurance)- the maximum level of compensation for claims against firms declared in default is 100% of the claim with no upper limit.
General insurance- general insurance advice and arranging is covered for 90% of the claim with no upper limit.  Protection is at 100% where claims arise in respect of compulsory insurance (e.g. employer's liability insurance), professional indemnity insurance and certain claims for injury, sickness or infirmity of the policyholder.
You can obtain more information about compensation scheme arrangements from the FSCS online at www.fscs.org.uk
