{"groupId":"CHK-009","requirement":"Where the Suitability Report contains a recommendation to replace, switch, transfer, consolidate, encash or surrender an existing product or investment, is this consistent with and supported by the evidence provided? Specifically: [G9.5] Switching costs exceed the benefits. Limb: Appropriateness. For every ceding plan the report compares existing against recommended, discloses the costs and benefits of switching, addresses safeguarded benefits and penalties, and considers alternatives — all corroborated by categories E and G.","reportSays":"The suitability report asserts four switching analyses with specific cost and benefit profiles: (1) Scottish Widows £211.32 (encashment with net receipt £170): no exit penalty, charge difference -0.06% / -£2.25, benefits stated as lower costs and greater choice. (2) Zurich £103,439.24: no exit penalty, charge difference -0.49% / -£506.85, benefits include lower costs, investment choice, multi-asset fund selection. (3) Standard Life £3,002.00: no exit penalty, charge difference +0.26% / +£268.94, higher costs justified by multi-asset and greater investment choice. (4) Aviva existing arrangement £3,744.36 mentioned with no formal cost analysis provided. Report states 'Like for Like' comparison shows Aviva plan 0.24% less expensive; 'Including Adviser Fee' shows 4.24% more expensive. Critical yield for Zurich analysis: 4.8% pa required to break even. Benefits cited across all plans: lower costs, greater investment choice, adviser charging facilitation, ongoing monitoring, lifestyling adjustment, enhanced retirement flexibility. Report claims benefits justify switching despite adviser fees increasing overall cost.","fileSays":"Pension switch report (P1-P8) corroborates the following: Three main comparisons (Zurich, Aviva, Standard Life) with side-by-side projected maturity values at low, mid and high growth rates. Zurich comparison (P7): Existing pension RIY 0.3%, New solution RIY 2.1% at low growth; RIY 2.3% at high growth. Critical yield 4.8% at mid growth (P7). Effect of switching: £10,400 decrease (9.6%) at low growth, £12,000 decrease (9.4%) at mid growth, £15,000 decrease (10.0%) at high growth. Standard Life comparison (P6): Existing pension RIY 0.6%, New solution RIY 0.6% (matching). Critical yield 6.0% for Standard Life only analysis. No figures matching report's claimed -0.49%/£506.85 for Zurich or +0.26%/£268.94 for Standard Life charge differences. Aviva comparison with all three retained: overall projected value £124,000 (P3). Immediate impact statement (P7): Fund shortfall of £3,305.00 on day one. No mention of Scottish Widows encashment analysis. Charge comparison on page P4 (Existing pensions vs. New solution table) shows new solution platform at 0.6% charge; Aviva retained at 0.59%; Zurich retained at 0.29%; all figures differ from report's switching cost assertions.","discrepancies":["Report asserts Zurich charge difference -0.49%/£506.85 annual saving; evidence (P7) shows Zurich existing RIY 0.3%, new solution RIY 2.1% (low growth), 2.2% (mid growth), 2.3% (high growth), implying new solution is MORE expensive, not less. The 0.26% increase claimed by report for Standard Life aligns directionally with evidence but the magnitude and basis are not independently verified in the passages.","Report asserts Scottish Widows -0.06%/£2.25 saving; no corresponding analysis found in evidence passages for this plan.","Report states 'Like for Like 0.24% less expensive' overall across all plans; evidence does not contain a consolidated charge comparison table matching this figure.","Report states 'Including Adviser Fee 4.24% more expensive' with derived figure of £4,672.00 required outperformance at 4.24%; this calculation basis is not shown in evidence.","Report asserts critical yield 1.9% for Scottish Widows and 7.8% for unspecified plan; evidence (P7) confirms 4.8% and 7.8% for Zurich but does not show 1.9% matching any named plan.","Immediate impact: 