{"groupId":"CHK-009","requirement":"[G9.9] Evidence elsewhere in the file that supports or contradicts the replacement rationale — Consistency: Where the Suitability Report contains a recommendation to replace, switch, transfer, consolidate, encash or surrender an existing product or investment, the rationale for that action must be supported by and consistent with evidence in the case file.","reportSays":"The report asserts four overarching benefits of switching: (1) 'lower costs, greater investment flexibility, and continued professional oversight' (page 7); (2) 'greater investment flexibility, improved retirement options, and continued professional oversight' (pages 7–8); (3) 'lower costs, greater investment flexibility, improved retirement options, and continued professional oversight' (page 8); and (4) 'This would not detract from your financial retirement plan' (page 6). Specific rationales for each plan are: (People's Pension) retain as workplace scheme with employer contributions; (Scottish Widows) encash under small pot rules for £170 net; (Aviva) lifestyling drift moves portfolio outside agreed risk range; (Zurich) risk level 5 unavailable, existing blend of risk 7 and 2 lacks diversification; (Standard Life) similar statement about lifestyling drift and risk misalignment.","fileSays":"[P5], [P6], [P20] (Pension Switch Report) provide a technical comparison across three existing arrangements (Aviva, Zurich, Standard Life) but show the new solution ranked 5th of 10 alternatives by maturity value at £125,000 vs. existing solution at £127,000 (a 1.6% decrease). The report shows 'Like for Like' savings of 0.24% in charges but 'Including Adviser Fee' costs increase by 4.24%. [P8] confirms Aviva holds 'Aviva Pensions My Future Focus Consolidation' with lifestyling; [P12] (Zurich illustration) shows retirement date 7 June 2026 (age 70, not 75 as stated in recommendations); [P16]–[P18] (file notes) record alternatives considered: Defaqto rates all People's Pension