{"groupId":"G10.4","requirement":"Vulnerability has a material impact on the recommendation (overlay)","reportSays":"The suitability report contains no extracted values at paths /vulnerability/perClient[]/impactOnRecommendation[] or /vulnerability/foreseeableHarms[]. The report does not assert any vulnerability, does not describe any support needs arising from vulnerability, and does not explain how vulnerability (if present) affects the suitability of the recommendation.","fileSays":"The case file contains evidence of multiple vulnerability indicators: (1) Client demonstrates very limited financial knowledge and investment understanding—passage [P1] shows responses of 'No understanding / knowledge' to questions about stocks and shares, enterprise schemes, venture capital trusts, and pension planning. The client has no investment experience in unit trusts, stocks and shares, or pension products. (2) Passage [P2] records 'No additional notes were recorded' in both Investor Experience and Capacity for Loss sections, indicating a potential assessment gap. (3) Passage [P14] describes the client's attitude to risk and capacity for loss: the client has 'limited' experience confined to 'workplace pension arrangements' and is 'not reliant upon pension funds'. (4) Passage [P6] records the client's stated need: 'Just needs advice helping him organise his pensions in the best place. Wants to consolidate to help him get his head around what he has.' This language suggests cognitive or organizational difficulty. (5) Passage [P3] and [P10] show the client's natural risk rating was 4 (Cautious Balanced) but was overridden to 5 (Balanced), confirmed in passage [P14]: 'You confirmed that you wish to increase your Risk rating to 5'. (6) Passage [P14] confirms capacity for loss: 'any potential underperformance would not have a detrimental impact on your day-to-day living' due to state pension and employment income. (7) Passage [P20] recommends 'It would also be prudent to set up and register Power of Attorney for your financial affairs / health and welfare, to ensure that in the event of your incapacity, your spouse or relative could act on your behalf'—flagging incapacity risk. (8) Passage [P12] shows current monthly disposable income is negative (£-288.00 monthly shortfall), indicating financial strain.","discrepancies":["Report asserts no vulnerability or support needs; file contains multiple indicators of limited financial knowledge, investment inexperience, and need for cognitive support to 'get his head around' his pensions.","Report does not reflect the client's very limited understanding of stocks, shares, pension planning, or investment risk (evidenced in [P1]).","Report does not reference or assess the gaps in Investor Experience or Capacity for Loss notes (both blank in [P2]), suggesting assessment may not have been documented.","Report overrides client's natural risk rating from 4 to 5 without explaining how this aligns with the client's stated limited understanding or need for consolidation support.","Report recommends Power of Attorney ([P20]) as a precaution but does not explain what vulnerability or incapacity concern this addresses.","Report does not assess whether the client's negative monthly cash flow (£-288 shortfall per [P12]) affects capacity to sustain the investment or creates vulnerability."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The comparison can be performed because the report's silence is explicit—the canonical model holds no values for vulnerability impact or foreseen harms—and the file contains clear evidence of circumstances that trigger FG21/1 vulnerability assessment obligations. The client exhibits multiple characteristics that should trigger vulnerability assessment: (1) Low financial capability—'No understanding / knowledge' across stocks, shares, pensions, and investment risk; (2) Limited investment experience—confined to workplace pension and cash accounts only; (3) Cognitive or organizational support need—stated as wanting help to 'get his head around what he has'; (4) Financial strain—negative monthly cash flow of £288 shortfall; (5) Age—69 years old, at life transition point (retirement in 2 years per [P6]); (6) Incapacity risk—report itself recommends Power of Attorney. These are classic FG21/1 drivers (low capability, life event, financial resilience concern, health/incapacity planning). The report overrides the client's natural cautious risk rating (4) to balanced (5) without addressing how this sits with his limited knowledge or consolidation need. Passage [P2] shows blank assessment notes for Investor Experience and Capacity for Loss, suggesting these sections were not engaged with meaningfully. Passage [P6] records the client's goal as consolidation and cognitive clarity, not growth. Passage [P14] confirms the client understands funds 'may go up as well as down' and is 'not reliant upon pension funds', yet does not explain why moving from a cautious to balanced risk profile aligns with someone of limited knowledge facing retirement. The critical issue is not whether vulnerability exists—the file strongly suggests it does—but that the report does not acknowledge it, assess it, or explain how the recommendation accounts for it. Where a report asserts no vulnerability but the file contains clear FG21/1 drivers and no documented assessment, the overlay assessment is unmet. The report's recommendation to consolidate pensions into a new Aviva platform with balanced-rated funds may be appropriate for a resilient client with investment knowledge, but no assessment demonstrates it is appropriate for this client's circumstances.","citations":[{"passageId":"P1","source":"D","category":"Risk profile report","quote":"Do you understand how stocks and shares work and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge. Do you understand how Enterprise Investment Schemes and Venture Capital Trusts work and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge. Do you understand how pension planning and income in retirement works and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P2","source":"D","category":"Risk profile report","quote":"No additional notes were recorded","cells":null},{"passageId":"P6","source":"B","category":"Fact Find","quote":"Just needs advice helping him organise his pensions in the best place. Wants to consolidate to help him get his head around what he has.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P12","source":"B","category":"Fact Find","quote":"Total Monthly Disposable Income £ -288.00","cells":null},{"passageId":"P14","source":"I","category":"Suitability Report","quote":"You completed an Attitude to Risk questionnaire. We felt that this didn't fully reflect your risk appetite. We agreed that you are a risk rating 5 rather than a 4 as per the questionnaire. John, you are aware that investment values can rise as well as fall, and although your experience is limited to your workplace pension arrangements, you understand that returns are not guaranteed.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P20","source":"I","category":"Suitability Report","quote":"It would also be prudent to set up and register Power of Attorney for your financial affairs / health and welfare, to ensure that in the event of your incapacity, your spouse or relative could act on your behalf.","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Missing evidence","Weak justification","Compliance concern"],"severity":"High","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

